  "statement": "The grid holds the characters 1 for land and 0 for water. An island is a group of land cells joined edge to edge, not diagonally. Return how many islands there are.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= rows, cols <= 300"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Scan every cell. When you hit land you have found a new island, so increment the counter.",
    "Then immediately flood the entire island so you never count it again, by depth-first or breadth-first search from that cell.",
    "The simplest flood overwrites each visited land cell with 0. Mutating the input is allowed here."
  ],
  "complexity": "O(rows * cols) time",
  "signature": "int Solve(char[][] grid)",
